One cluster = One big pool of resources? Wrong.

Most people treat a Kubernetes cluster as one giant space.
- All workloads mixed together.
- All teams sharing the same environment.

That leads to conflicts and chaos.
Namespaces let you organize your cluster into isolated sections.

With Namespaces:
- Avoid naming collisions
- Apply RBAC for team-level access
- Enforce quotas and limits
- Keep things clean and organized
